as thickening dishes. It is made by grinding grains, beans, nuts, seeds, roots, or vegetables using a mill."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-potato-flour"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Potato_flour"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Ainu cuisine","cuisine/ainu-cuisine",[["Munini-imo","dish/munini-imo"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Potato starch","ingredient/potato-starch"]]}]},"dish/quarkkaulchen":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/quarkkaulchen","n":"Quarkkäulchen","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Saxon cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Quarkkäulchen is a Saxon dish made from dough containing about two-thirds mashed potatoes, one-third quark cheese, eggs and flour, and perhaps spiced with cinnamon or dotted with raisins. The dough is fried in butter or clarified butter into small pancakes. These are served hot, usually with sugar, fruits or other sweet side dishes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-quarkkaulchen"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quarkk%C3%A4ulchen"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Saxon cuisine","cuisine/saxon-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":6,"links":[["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Quark","ingredient/quark"],["Quark (cheese)","ingredient/quark-cheese"],["Raisin","ingredient/raisin"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"]]},{"h":"More from Saxon cuisine","links":[["Stollen","dish/stollen"]]}]},"dish/sopa-paraguaya":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/sopa-paraguaya","n":"Sopa paraguaya","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Paraguayan cuisine","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["Sopa paraguaya (Spanish for 'Paraguayan soup') is a traditional food in Paraguayan cuisine similar to corn bread, spongy and soft. Corn flour, cheese, onion and milk or whey are common ingredients. It is a cake rich in caloric and protein content."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-sopa-paraguaya"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sopa_paraguaya"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Paraguayan cuisine","cuisine/paraguayan-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":7,"links":[["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Cornmeal","ingredient/cornmeal"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Maize flour","ingredient/maize-flour"],["Milk","ingredient/milk"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Paraguay cheese","ingredient/paraguay-cheese"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Camila Made: Top 15 Paraguayan Recipes","ref":"site/camilamade-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"camilamade.com","note":"Paraguayan recipe roundup on a Latin American home cooking blog.","url":"https://camilamade.com/top-15-paraguayan-recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Paraguayan cuisine","links":[["Chipá","dish/chipa"],["Dulce de batata","dish/dulce-de-batata"],["Paraguay cheese","dish/paraguay-cheese"],["Piracaldo","dish/piracaldo"]]}]},"dish/stigghiola":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/stigghiola","n":"Stigghiola","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Sicilian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["The stigghiola, also known as stigghiuola, is a Sicilian food typical of the streets of the city of Palermo. It consists of guts (usually of lamb, but also of goat or chicken) which are washed in water and salt, seasoned with parsley and often with onion and other pot herbs, then stuck on a skewer or rolled around a leek, and finally cooked directly on the grill. The dish is generally prepared and sold as a street food. In Ragusa, the dish is baked in a casserole and is known as turciniuna."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-stigghiola"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stigghiola"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Sicilian cuisine","cuisine/sicilian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Intestine","ingredient/intestine"]]},{"h":"More fr